      "key_point": "S4.K2",
      "question": "Besides using a handheld controller, what other body parts can be used to control the pointing ray?",
      "answer": "Pointing can be achieved through head movement (head pointing) or by tracking the user's eye gaze using specialized eye trackers."
    },
    {
      "key_point": "S4.K3",
      "question": "What is the primary mechanism of the bend cast technique, and what problem does it aim to solve?",
      "answer": "Bend cast bends the virtual ray toward the object closest to its path, which helps reduce the need for precise aiming when selecting targets."
