{
  "recap": "To create effective sound effects in VR, developers must first understand how perception works. This involves studying psychophysics, which examines perceptual phenomena produced by physical stimuli, and psychoacoustics, which focuses specifically on acoustic stimuli. Key concepts like Stevens' power law and the Just Noticeable Difference (JND) help quantify how we perceive changes in magnitude.",
  "review": [
